{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"RCA (2026-09-08): sibling_exclusive_lock guards neither import-time absence nor runtime use of fcntl. The function-local import makes POSIX collection safe but still raises ModuleNotFoundError on Windows as soon as HLC/sidecar/recent-create paths enter the context manager. The correct fix is to route blocking sibling locks through the existing kernel lock abstraction rather than open-coding fcntl in fsutil."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788857758040881001,"uuid":"25db48ae-40ef-4c02-a165-83c81acbc5af"}